/P 132 0 R
/E (Existing feature selection methods rank sensors using a single snapshot of data, assuming that sensor importance remains constant over time. However, in semiconductor manufacturing, sensor behavior changes due to process drift, making these methods unreliable for long-term fault prediction. This challenge is further compounded by the highly imbalanced nature of the data, where failure samples are rare.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
